From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:13:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: exynos9820-beyond2lte: Enable Wi-Fi

The Wi-Fi half of the BCM4375 on this board sits on the first PCIe
controller, and comes up on a line of its own, WL_REG_ON on gpg0-5: the
vendor board tree hands that line to its Wi-Fi driver (the wlan node) and
also lists it in the default pin state of the controller, and its PCIe
driver raises it and waits 100 ms before it trains the link.

Describe the line as a fixed regulator with that start-up delay and the pin
settings of the vendor (output, no pull, drive 3, keep the level in sleep),
hand it to the controller as its endpoint supply, and enable the
controller.

Measured on a Galaxy S10+: with the Wi-Fi firmware in the initramfs,
wlan0 comes up by itself at boot, and a scan sees networks on both
2.4 GHz and 5 GHz.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts | 39 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
index df360473eac..a97def1a6f5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
@@ -443,6 +443,16 @@ &oscclk {
 	clock-frequency = <26000000>;
 };
 
+/*
+ * The Wi-Fi half of the BCM4375 sits on this controller.  It answers only
+ * once the line below has powered it up, so that line is the supply the
+ * controller switches on before it releases the chip from reset.
+ */
+&pcie0 {
+	vpcie3v3-supply = <&wlan_reg_on>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &pinctrl_alive {
 	key_volup: key-volup-pins {
 		samsung,pins = "gpa0-3";
@@ -498,6 +508,17 @@ pmic_irq: pmic-irq-pins {
 	};
 };
 
+&pinctrl_peric0 {
+	wlan_en_pins: wlan-en-pins {
+		samsung,pins = "gpg0-5";
+		samsung,pin-function = <EXYNOS_PIN_FUNC_OUTPUT>;
+		samsung,pin-pud = <EXYNOS_PIN_PULL_NONE>;
+		samsung,pin-drv = <EXYNOS5420_PIN_DRV_LV4>;
+		samsung,pin-con-pdn = <EXYNOS_PIN_PDN_PREV>;
+		samsung,pin-pud-pdn = <EXYNOS_PIN_PULL_NONE>;
+	};
+};
+
 / {
 	reg_usb_dummy: regulator-usb-dummy {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
@@ -505,6 +526,24 @@ reg_usb_dummy: regulator-usb-dummy {
 	};
 };
 
+/ {
+	/*
+	 * WL_REG_ON, the line that powers up the Wi-Fi half of the BCM4375.
+	 * The Bluetooth half has a line of its own.  The vendor raises this
+	 * one and waits 100 ms before the controller may train the link, and
+	 * keeps its level through sleep.
+	 */
+	wlan_reg_on: regulator-wlan-en {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "wlan_en";
+		gpio = <&gpg0 5 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		startup-delay-us = <100000>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&wlan_en_pins>;
+	};
+};
+
 &serial0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
